 "text": "Hey, how are things with her? Stand flat footed on something tall, like a door frame. If your bike's seat is level, the back of your seat will be straight ahead. Stand with your feet shoulder width apart, and lean slightly forwards so you standing on your tiptoes. The back of the seat will be straight ahead. That's normal when sitting. The seat tube blocks the back of the seat. Lower the seat so it level, then add a small cushion. Most seats drop a couple of inches after you sit on them. You' still be close. If it bothers, try a shorter stem that turns the handlebars a bit",
